---
import Console from "../layouts/Console.astro";
import Island from "../layouts/Island.astro";
---

<Console
  title="Components"
  lede="The registry, grouped by helix node. Read live from the API, so what you see is what a consumer would install right now."
>
  {/*
    The fallback names `api.mzizi.dev` because that is now what the island
    reads (`api::DEFAULT_API_BASE`). It said so before the host existed, which
    made it a true-sounding sentence about a dead address; it is true on
    purpose now.

    NOTE the second half: `mzizi.dev/components` is a REGISTRY page, and it
    200s only while the apex is still the Next.js registry. When the apex
    becomes `mzizi-dev/mzizi-site`, this no-JS escape hatch 404s — the static
    site has no /components. Re-point it as part of that cutover; see the
    runbook in mzizi-site/README.md.
  */}
  <Island
    name="components"
    fallback="The component list is read from api.mzizi.dev at runtime, so it needs scripting. Browse it at mzizi.dev/components instead."
  />
</Console>
